#
# The serial console shell must not start by itself.
#
# AOSP starts it on every userdebug build, in system/core/rootdir/init.rc:
#
#     on init && property:ro.debuggable=1
#         start console
#
# and LineageOS builds userdebug, so we get it running. It is a "user shell"
# (not root) on /dev/console, that is on the UART: anyone with physical access
# to the test pads gets a prompt without having to unlock anything. Useful
# during bring-up, not on a phone in someone's hands.
#
# The kernel console stays on, though -- printk still comes out on ttyMT3, and
# it is the only trace available when the system dies before opening logd. That
# is identical to the stock kernel (CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y and
# "console=tty0 console=ttyMT3,921600n1" in CONFIG_CMDLINE): that is untouched
# here, only the shell goes away.
#
# Why "on init" works from /system/etc/init: since Android 11 init parses that
# directory right after init.rc (init.cpp, ParseConfig("/system/etc/init")), no
# longer as a late import. Actions are queued in the order the files were read,
# so this "stop" runs right after AOSP's "start", within the same trigger. The
# "stop" leaves the service marked SVC_DISABLED, so it does not come back up
# with the "class_start core" in "on boot".
#
# To turn it back on when needed, without rebuilding anything:
#     adb root && adb shell start console
# or, from init, a "setprop ctl.start console".

on init
    stop console
